# TIS-Summary — Project Workflow

## Start every session by reading these four files

```
~/Projects/TIS-Summary/memory.md       — family, children, school contacts, credentials
~/Projects/TIS-Summary/architecture.md — system components and data flow
~/Projects/TIS-Summary/decisions.md    — why things were built the way they were
~/Projects/TIS-Summary/todo.md         — open next steps
```

Do not rely on chat history. These files are the project's permanent knowledge base.

## Knowledge file update protocol

Whenever you make a significant decision, update the relevant file **and notify Fredrik immediately**:

| What changed | Update |
|---|---|
| New school fact, contact, credential, family note | `memory.md` |
| System structure, component, data flow | `architecture.md` |
| Technical or design decision with rationale | `decisions.md` |
| Work item added, completed, or cancelled | `todo.md` |

Never silently update project knowledge. Always tell Fredrik which file was modified and what changed.

## Design-before-coding discipline

Before writing any UI code:

1. What is the purpose of this screen / section?
2. What is the primary user action?
3. What is the information hierarchy?
4. Which SDK components serve this content best?
5. Plan the layout.
6. Then implement.

Never start with a `<Stack>` of raw data. Think first.

## Quality standard

Every canvas must look like a polished, production-ready dashboard — comparable to Google Workspace, Linear, or Notion. Ask yourself before finishing:

- Does this look like something Google would ship?
- Is the hierarchy immediately obvious?
- Would I proudly include this in a portfolio?

If the answer to any of these is "no", keep improving.

## Definition of done

A canvas run is complete only when:

- [ ] All data for the target week is extracted and deduplicated
- [ ] Canvas renders without TypeScript errors
- [ ] Layout follows the M3 design system (see `canvas-design-system.mdc`)
- [ ] A short chat recap lists the actions that cannot wait
- [ ] Any new school facts are added to `memory.md`
- [ ] Fredrik has been notified of any knowledge file updates
